id: pm-todos-zbe0
title: Publish attestation gate misses a publish routed through a declaration keyword or a braced expansion
description: "The gate resolves a command held in a shell variable so a publish routed through one is still audited, but it skipped a command position that still held an expansion. Two independent holes let an unattested publish through while an attested sibling in the same file satisfied the non-vacuity check. First, the scalar indexer takes a binding written bare or with export only, so readonly NPM=npm, declare NPM=npm, typeset NPM=npm and local NPM=npm all left the NPM binding unindexed and the publish invisible. Second, the tokenizer treated the brace of a parameter expansion as a brace-group separator, so a braced expansion in command position split into three words and read as a command named publish. Both were confirmed by executing the gate, not by reading it."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-05T20:35:32.924Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-05T20:35:58.868Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-05T20:35:58.834Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-05T20:35:58.834Z"
author: codex
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "A publish routed through any declaration keyword or a braced expansion is audited, and an attested sibling in the same file cannot cover for it."
actual_result: "readonly, declare, typeset and local left the binding unindexed and the publish invisible, and a braced expansion in command position split into three words and read as a command named publish; with an attested sibling present the gate reported every invocation as attested."
tests[2]:
  - command: node --test test/verify-release-publish-attestation.test.ts
    path: test/verify-release-publish-attestation.test.ts
    scope: project
    provenance:
      author: codex
      created_at: "2026-09-05T20:35:43.738Z"
      source_kind: local_mutation
      source_ref: fix/index-unquoted-scalar-assignments
    assert_stdout_contains[1]: pass 71
    note: "Ten added cases pair every hidden publish with an ATTESTED sibling, so each one fails against the unfixed gate for the right reason rather than tripping the non-vacuity check. Reverting the fail-closed check alone fails 8 of them; reverting the tokenizer brace fix alone fails 1; both present pass 71 with 0 failures."
  - command: "npm run verify:release-publish-attestation"
    path: .github/workflows/release.yml
    scope: project
    provenance:
      author: codex
      created_at: "2026-09-05T20:35:43.738Z"
      source_kind: local_mutation
      source_ref: fix/index-unquoted-scalar-assignments
    assert_stdout_contains[1]: every publish invocation is attested
    note: "The repository's own release workflow still passes the tightened gate, so the fail-closed refusal did not become a false positive on real usage."
docs[2]{path,scope,note}:
  scripts/shell-command-scan.ts,project,Consumes a balanced parameter expansion as one word so a braced expansion in command position is not split into three
  scripts/verify-release-publish-attestation.ts,project,"Audits an unresolved command position instead of skipping it, so a declaration keyword nobody enumerated is covered too"
close_reason: "Two independent fixes, each verified load-bearing by reverting it alone. The candidate loop now audits a command position that still holds an expansion rather than skipping it, which is the property itself rather than a list of keywords, so a shape nobody has enumerated is covered too. The tokenizer consumes a balanced parameter expansion as one word. All 273 tests pass and release:check passes end to end; the repository's own release workflow still passes the tightened gate."
body: ""
